00:39:52.730 --> 00:39:53.690
Did you edit it out?

00:39:53.690 --> 00:39:54.500
What happened?

00:39:54.500 --> 00:39:55.530
No, this is real.

00:39:55.530 --> 00:39:59.840
If you don't believe me, stop
by the booth in the Startup

00:39:59.840 --> 00:40:01.970
Village and we'll
show you it in action.

00:40:01.970 --> 00:40:04.430
But this kind of response
with this complexity,

00:40:04.430 --> 00:40:06.950
without the need to
transform your data,

00:40:06.950 --> 00:40:10.240
has never been done before.

00:40:10.240 --> 00:40:15.700
And so next question
is, why Google Cloud?

00:40:15.700 --> 00:40:17.879
Well, there's a few things here.

00:40:17.879 --> 00:40:19.420
One of the things
that we notice when

00:40:19.420 --> 00:40:22.300
we're speaking with our
customers is elastic scaling.

00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:25.330
We definitely wanted to have
a system and a platform that

00:40:25.330 --> 00:40:28.300
enabled us to grow with the
demands of our customers.

00:40:28.300 --> 00:40:30.190
We have customers
here in San Francisco

00:40:30.190 --> 00:40:31.840
like [? hypergrowth ?]
startups that

00:40:31.840 --> 00:40:34.180
are kind of like
Spotify for clothes

00:40:34.180 --> 00:40:38.232
that are providing analytics to
their users using this system.

00:40:38.232 --> 00:40:39.940
Of course at different
parts of the year,

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:41.648
they are going to have
different demands.

00:40:41.648 --> 00:40:44.050
And to be able to spin up
and grow your system in less

00:40:44.050 --> 00:40:48.640
than 10 minutes is something
that was really, really unique.

00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:49.987
Also, price performance.

00:40:49.987 --> 00:40:51.320
A lot of talk about performance.

00:40:51.320 --> 00:40:54.650
But really it's going to come
down to a predictable cost.

00:40:54.650 --> 00:40:57.470
Can I know exactly what this
is going to cost me next month

00:40:57.470 --> 00:40:59.845
or am I going to be
guessing what my budget?

00:40:59.845 --> 00:41:00.970
How do I budget for this?

00:41:00.970 --> 00:41:02.230
How do I plan?

00:41:02.230 --> 00:41:05.630
And that's where Incorta felt
that Google Cloud was very,

00:41:05.630 --> 00:41:09.550
very straightforward but
also a very good price

00:41:09.550 --> 00:41:11.774
point for performance.

00:41:11.774 --> 00:41:14.190
And the third one, no shock
here at Google right, but this

00:41:14.190 --> 00:41:15.600
would be developer friendly.

00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:17.280
Probably everyone
here might well

00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:21.060
be from a developer background
and it doesn't stop here.

00:41:21.060 --> 00:41:22.770
It's very unlikely
that you would

00:41:22.770 --> 00:41:27.180
get invited to even speak
into the direction of a cloud

00:41:27.180 --> 00:41:29.260
company as a startup.

00:41:29.260 --> 00:41:31.800
And we have found that to be
very true with our relationship

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:34.040
with Google Cloud.

00:41:34.040 --> 00:41:36.660
And so I want to talk about
one of those things that

00:41:36.660 --> 00:41:39.270
has come out of this
relationship with Google Cloud

00:41:39.270 --> 00:41:41.149
that we think is super exciting.

00:41:41.149 --> 00:41:42.690
So here, I'm glad
to announce that we

00:41:42.690 --> 00:41:45.990
have a special way
for enterprises

00:41:45.990 --> 00:41:48.060
to get to the Cloud.

00:41:48.060 --> 00:41:50.460
Now, we have a lot
of enterprises that

00:41:50.460 --> 00:41:52.290
historically have data centers.

00:41:52.290 --> 00:41:54.540
If you've been around for
probably more than 10 years,

00:41:54.540 --> 00:41:56.160
you probably have a data center.

00:41:56.160 --> 00:41:58.330
And you probably know, I
want to get to the cloud,

00:41:58.330 --> 00:41:59.637
but how do I get there?

00:41:59.637 --> 00:42:01.470
Am I going to take
everything down and move,

00:42:01.470 --> 00:42:03.030
or do I want to do it in pieces?

00:42:03.030 --> 00:42:07.800
Or how can I augment what I have
with some additional resources

00:42:07.800 --> 00:42:09.226
from the Cloud?

00:42:09.226 --> 00:42:11.450
And so Incorta
provides the ability

00:42:11.450 --> 00:42:15.080
to have a single dashboard and
have different components that

00:42:15.080 --> 00:42:17.450
look to the user seamless.

00:42:17.450 --> 00:42:19.450
They're just getting
served content.

00:42:19.450 --> 00:42:21.530
Where that content
is coming from

00:42:21.530 --> 00:42:24.070
could be Incorta
running on Google Cloud

00:42:24.070 --> 00:42:27.290
or it could be Incorta running
on your own data centers.

00:42:27.290 --> 00:42:29.960
So content that maybe you're
not prepared to yet put

00:42:29.960 --> 00:42:32.840
in the Cloud, you can
keep it on your premises

00:42:32.840 --> 00:42:34.760
locally in your data center.

00:42:34.760 --> 00:42:36.350
But data maybe that
you want to use

00:42:36.350 --> 00:42:38.330
for other teams or
other people to be

00:42:38.330 --> 00:42:40.846
able to leverage
the power of Incorta

00:42:40.846 --> 00:42:43.220
on that platform to be able
to do that with Google Cloud.

00:42:43.220 --> 00:42:44.636
And to give you
that extensibility

00:42:44.636 --> 00:42:50.030
to grow and to shrink as
needed when demands are met.

00:42:50.030 --> 00:42:53.810
So with that, I'd like to
invite you to come speak to us.

00:42:53.810 --> 00:42:56.294
We will be at the Startup
Village for a few more hours.

00:42:56.294 --> 00:42:57.710
And if you're
unable to make that,

00:42:57.710 --> 00:42:59.960
definitely start by Incorta.com.

00:42:59.960 --> 00:43:03.740
We'd love to show you a demo
and to talk more about that.

00:43:03.740 --> 00:43:06.790
[MUSIC PLAYING]

